# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .dockerignore — controls the build context sent to `COPY . .` in Dockerfile
# Grouped by category, ordered from largest / most volatile to least.
# NOTE: order carries no meaning here except that `!` re-includes must come
# after their corresponding exclude. Keep this file grouped, not append-only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- VCS / CI metadata ---
.git
.github
.gitignore
.editorconfig

# --- Build artifacts (largest and most volatile first) ---
# Cloned OpenWrt source tree (multi-GB), never part of the image
lede/
# Logs and generated release notes produced by prepare_build.sh / generate-release.sh
**/*.log
release.generated.md

# --- Temp / cache junk ---
*.tmp
*.swp
.DS_Store
.ccache
**/__pycache__

# --- Editor directories ---
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Docs (LICENSE intentionally kept so the image retains license info) ---
README.md

# --- Docker files themselves ---
# BuildKit reads these separately, so excluding them never breaks the build;
# it only keeps them out of `COPY . .`.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
